Scripted Curl POST of Hardcoded Credentials to Tunnel /login Endpoint

This threat hunting scenario detects curl processes submitting hardcoded username and password parameters to a /login endpoint hosted on known tunneling infrastructure, including ngrok, Cloudflare Quick Tunnel, and localhost.run domains. The combination of scripted HTTP POST activity, credential-like parameters, and externally exposed tunnel infrastructure is suspicious because attackers can use temporary tunnels to receive credentials from compromised systems or facilitate unauthorized communication with attacker-controlled services.

From a threat-hunting perspective, the focus is on identifying unusual curl → external tunnel → /login activity and determining whether the submitted credentials belong to local users, applications, services, or other systems. Analysts should correlate the command line with the initiating process, script or file that executed curl, user context, DNS/network activity, and any preceding or subsequent tunnel-related activity. Particular attention should be given to endpoints that also exhibit cloudflared, ngrok, or other tunneling-tool execution, as this may indicate a broader attack chain involving credential collection and unauthorized external access.

MITRE ATT&CK Mapping:

T1552.001 – Unsecured Credentials: Credentials In Files
T1071.001 – Application Layer Protocol: Web Protocols

dataset = xdr_data
| filter event_type = ENUM.PROCESS and event_sub_type = ENUM.PROCESS_START
| filter action_process_image_path ~= "(?i).*[/\\]curl$"
| filter action_process_image_command_line contains "/login"
| filter (action_process_image_command_line contains "user=" or action_process_image_command_line contains "username=")
| filter action_process_image_command_line contains "password="
| filter (action_process_image_command_line contains "ngrok.io" or action_process_image_command_line contains "ngrok-free.app" or action_process_image_command_line contains "trycloudflare.com" or action_process_image_command_line contains "lhr.life")
| fields _time, agent_hostname, action_process_image_command_line, actor_process_command_line
